REOPENED 2026-08-15 (AzureBay): this was sitting in_progress with ZERO commits referencing it since 2026-08-04 — claimed and abandoned, not worked. Reopened rather than closed, because nothing landed and fabricating a closure would be worse than admitting it.

It is the worst measured loss in the bank and it now has a much narrower target than when it was filed. Evidence from bd-ha71t / bd-2pq73 / bd-yu6jz, all counted, all this session:
  * the kernel issues TWO uncached security.capability getxattr probes per path-based metadata op, one on the mount ROOT (ino=1) and one on the target inode, independent of path depth (intermediate directories are never probed);
  * suppression is closed by measurement — ENOSYS is per-connection, FUSE_HANDLE_KILLPRIV V1 and V2 both negotiated and INERT;
  * the daemon-side answer is now ~free: 4001 of 4001 probes served from the capability memo on a warm read-write mount, format-level lookups cut 2000 -> 50 on a 50-file sweep;
  * on a warm mount there is NO other FUSE traffic — no getattr, no lookup — because the 60s attr TTL keeps them cached.

So whatever remains of this 8.32x is FUSE transport and per-request handling, not filesystem work. Anyone picking this up should start from readdir+stat request counts per directory entry rather than from the format layer, and should NOT re-attempt probe suppression.

